======================================================================
5. CONSTITUTIVE MODEL
======================================================================

The recovered COMSOL documentation specifies an anisotropic,
Holzapfel–Ogden-type myocardial solid-mechanics formulation.

The computational representation is intended to capture passive
anisotropic myocardial mechanical behavior within a finite-element
framework.

The formulation is treated as nearly incompressible.

The exact numerical material coefficients must be taken from the
controlled model implementation/parameter record.

Where an exact coefficient cannot be recovered from an executable model,
native COMSOL file, or authoritative parameter record, it must remain
classified as:

NOT CURRENTLY RECOVERED

No material parameter should be reconstructed solely from a desired
manuscript result.

======================================================================
6. COMPUTATIONAL DOMAIN
======================================================================

The computational domain consists of the patient-specific ventricular
solid geometry represented as a volumetric finite-element model.

Anatomically defined ventricular and great-vessel surfaces may be
partitioned into regions for application of the prescribed mechanical
and loading conditions.

The computational domain and boundary definitions should remain fixed
across the primary gravity sweep unless a specific sensitivity analysis
explicitly modifies the relevant parameter.

Figure 2 / Supplementary Figure S2 should describe the actual implemented
computational domain and boundary surfaces.

The figure must not contain boundary-condition labels such as:

"z-periodic"
"y-periodic"
"x-radiative"

unless those conditions are confirmed to exist in the actual COMSOL model.

The manuscript-facing description should instead identify the actual
anatomical boundary regions and their corresponding mechanical/loading
roles.

======================================================================
7. BOUNDARY CONDITIONS AND LOADING
======================================================================

The recovered computational framework includes:

- ventricular mechanical constraints
- anatomically defined basal constraint(s)
- cavity loading
- gravity-dependent body-force loading.

The exact implementation of the basal constraint and any spring/damper
parameters must be reconciled with the final COMSOL model before being
reported as exact numerical model parameters.

The exact cavity-pressure parameter is also not currently recovered in the
available documentation.

Therefore:

Cavity pressure:
SPECIFIED AS A MODEL INPUT
EXACT NUMERICAL VALUE: NOT CURRENTLY RECOVERED

Basal mechanical constraint:
SPECIFIED AS A MODEL COMPONENT
EXACT NUMERICAL IMPLEMENTATION: REQUIRES RECONCILIATION

No unsupported numerical value should be inserted into the manuscript.

