8. GRAVITY EXPERIMENT
======================================================================

The controlled gravity experiment consists of six predefined gravitational
conditions:

G01 = 1.00 g
G02 = 0.75 g
G03 = 0.50 g
G04 = 0.38 g
G05 = 0.16 g
G06 = 0.00 g

The primary comparison therefore progresses from terrestrial gravity toward
microgravity:

1.00
 ->
0.75
 ->
0.50
 ->
0.38
 ->
0.16
 ->
0.00 g

For visualization, the gravity axis is ordered from 1.00 g to 0.00 g,
descending left to right.

The gravity-dependent loading is introduced through the predefined
gravitational body-force condition / gravity multiplier.

The principal patient-specific model configuration is held constant across
the primary gravity sweep unless a controlled sensitivity analysis
explicitly modifies a model parameter.

