11. NONLINEAR SOLVER
======================================================================

The recovered computational framework specifies a Newton-type nonlinear
solution strategy for the finite-element model.

Solver convergence should be evaluated using the predefined numerical
convergence criteria and residual assessment.

Previously documented residual values are not automatically treated as
verified solver outputs.

The underlying solver log or equivalent COMSOL execution record should be
retained where available.

======================================================================
12. PRIMARY COMPUTATIONAL OUTPUTS
======================================================================

The six primary computational endpoints are:

A. Peak von Mises myocardial stress
   Units: kPa

B. Peak principal strain
   Units: %

C. Maximum ventricular displacement
   Units: mm

D. LV cavity volume
   Units: mL

E. Ventricular strain energy
   Units: J

F. Normalized response
   Units: %

The normalized response is calculated relative to the 1.00 g value:

Normalized response =
value at specified gravity /
value at 1.00 g
x 100.

For the baseline condition:

1.00 g = 100% reference.

This normalization must use the corresponding endpoint's value at 1.00 g
as its denominator.

